<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $141.9 mln Feb 18.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $141.9 mln Feb 18.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $141.9 million surplus on Feb 18 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 18</p>
<p>Exports: $215 million</p>
<p>Imports: $192.8 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $285.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $165.5 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $141.9 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.820 million</p>
<p>Imports: $1.659 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.299 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $1.738 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $722 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418))</p>
</text>
